solution:
**Given:**

sqrt{2}csc A = 2sec A

**Formula used:**

cosec A = 1/sin A, sec A = 1/cos A

1 + tan²A = sec²A

**Calculations:**

⇒ dfrac{sqrt{2}}{sin A}=dfrac{2}{cos A} (Given)

⇒ sqrt{2}cos A=2sin A

⇒ tan A=dfrac{sin A}{cos A}=dfrac{sqrt{2}}{2}=dfrac{1}{sqrt{2}}

⇒ sec² A=1+tan² A=1+dfrac{1}{2}=dfrac{3}{2}

⇒ sec A=sqrt{dfrac{3}{2}}

⇒ tan A times sec A=dfrac{1}{sqrt{2}}timessqrt{dfrac{3}{2}}=dfrac{sqrt{3}}{2}

**∴ tanA × secA = dfrac{sqrt{3}}{2}**
